@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security;architecture] explore-is-public-with-an-owned-lifetime
Explore MUST show anonymous Popular/search and public repository PR pages without
Access credentials or account sign-in. It MUST consume only the explicit tokenless
public client, never legacy Inbox/review stores or AI authority. Its route state MUST
cancel replaced requests, ignore stale results/errors and reject retired callbacks;
source retirement MUST clear inputs and rows. A popped public page MAY retain inert
rows only through its exit animation; popped callbacks/results MUST already be revoked.
Public repository selection and pagination MUST
retain the selected immutable repository ID, and a confirmed visibility/identity denial
MUST clear prior PR rows. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 signed-out browsing and personal
GitHub request, approved direct-native guest slice and public-boundary review.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] fresh-entry-does-not-inherit-a-private-workspace
A fresh/reinstalled native app without matching verified existing-connection evidence
MUST open Explore, even if a restored preference selected the existing-server entry.
A legitimate returning connection MUST retain its existing workspace unless the user
chose public browsing. That choice MUST preserve the saved private account. Selecting
another entry MUST revoke retained callbacks and pending results before mounting its
pages; returning to Explore MUST NOT revive a previous guest source. Public startup
MUST NOT instantiate private Home, account discovery, AI or Stats observers. Source:
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 reinstall screenshot and no-sign-in public browsing request.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] guest-links-keep-public-and-private-authority-separate
Guest links MUST use the same Compose navigation stack and MUST NOT mount private
review/repository clients. Until native public review exists, a verified-format GitHub
link MAY offer an explicit fixed-origin Open on GitHub action. Private/server links
MUST offer the existing-account entry or public browsing without fetching private data.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 public browsing decision, nav-links-inside-open-like-outside
and the approved staged public list/PR implementation.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;architecture] explore-reuses-pully-and-the-shared-stack
Android and iOS MUST use the same Explore state and presentation, Pully's existing
design kit and the host's shared Compose route stack. Opening a repository MUST use
the host navigation callback; Explore MUST NOT create an independent native/child
back stack. The initial list slice MUST label PR actions as opening GitHub until a
public review route actually exists. Account invitations MUST reflect real server
sign-in capability rather than inventing OAuth success or sending operator secrets.
Source: mobile-reuses-production-ui, shared-navigation-keeps-one-compose-stack and
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 guest browsing/personal sign-in request.
